            },
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Where are we on a sphere?</h3>In a previous lesson, we learned to locate ourselves on a flat disk. Now, let’s try a practical exercise:</p><p><center><div class=\"first_steps_lab_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_lab question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-microscope\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_lab\"><b>Creating a Sphere</b><br /><br />Draw a circle on a sheet of paper — a plate makes a good guide; trace around it with a pencil. Then cut out the circle. Place it flat in front of you, like a plate on a table. Now spin it around a diameter that lies in the disk’s plane: as the disk turns, it sweeps out a ball whose boundary is a sphere!</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
