               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 500\" role=\"img\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto; max-width:760px; display:block; margin:0 auto;\" aria-label=\"Three-dimensional axes X, Y and Z inside a transparent quarter of a sphere. A red vector leaves the flat plane and reaches a point P on the curved surface of the quarter sphere. The values are shown in linear coordinates x = 4, y = 3 and z = 5; the XY projection P′ is 5 meters from O at theta = 37 degrees, while the full vector P has spherical coordinates r = 7.1, theta = 37 degrees and phi = 45 degrees\"><text x=\"20\" y=\"428\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#333333\">Linear: (x, y, z) = (4 m, 3 m, 5 m)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"452\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#333333\">XY projection P′: (5 m, 37°)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"476\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#333333\">Spherical: (r, θ, φ) = (7.1 m, 37°, 45°)</text><polygon points=\"300,360 600,400 693.5,230.0 393.5,190.0\" fill=\"#eaf2fa\" stroke=\"#b9cde3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><defs><radialGradient id=\"a494d959SphereGrad\" cx=\"0.32\" cy=\"0.22\" r=\"1.05\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#ffffff\" stop-opacity=\"0.55\"/><stop offset=\"45%\" stop-color=\"#a9c9e8\" stop-opacity=\"0.28\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#2f6fb3\" stop-opacity=\"0.10\"/></radialGradient></defs><g id=\"sphericalOctant\"><path d=\"M 300.0,360.0 L 300.0,7.0 A 353.0 353.0 0 0 1 649.9,406.7 Z\" fill=\"url(#a494d959SphereGrad)\" stroke=\"#4f8bc4\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-opacity=\"0.9\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M 300.0,28.2 A 331.8 331.8 0 0 1 628.9,403.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\"/><path d=\"M 300.0,360.0 L 489.8,62.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4f8bc4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.22\"/><path d=\"M 300.0,360.0 L 620.1,211.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4f8bc4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.2