\"569.0\" y=\"112.0\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#333333\">P</text><text x=\"567.0\" y=\"264.0\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#333333\">P′</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#c0392b\">r</text></svg></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 5</b>: The same vector outside the flat plane. In linear coordinates it has x = 4 m, y = 3 m and z = 5 m; the XY projection P′ is 5 m from O at θ ≈ 37°; the full vector P has spherical coordinates r = 7.1 m, θ ≈ 37° and φ = 45°. A transparent quarter of the sphere, of radius r, is drawn around O, so you can check the spherical coordinates inside it.</p>",
